# Standalone backend container configuration for development/testing only.
# The office server deployment is configured from ../log-infra/.env instead.
#
# Redis host/port reachable FROM the logstream container. How you fill these in
# depends on how Redis is actually deployed relative to this app:
#
#   1. Bundled docker-compose service (default below) — Redis runs as the
#      "redis" service in this same compose file, reachable by Docker's
#      internal DNS on the shared network. No port needs to be published
#      to the host. Just leave REDIS_HOST=redis.
#
#   2. A separate container/service on the SAME Docker network (not the one
#      bundled here) — REDIS_HOST is that container's name or network alias,
#      same idea as #1 but pointing at infra this repo doesn't own.
#
#   3. A separate host/VM, reachable over the network — REDIS_HOST is its
#      DNS name or IP, REDIS_PORT whatever it listens on. Requires the port
#      open between the two hosts (firewall/security group), and Redis bound
#      to an interface that accepts remote connections, not just 127.0.0.1.
#
#   4. A managed/cloud Redis (ElastiCache, Azure Cache, Redis Cloud, etc.) —
#      REDIS_HOST/REDIS_PORT/REDIS_PASSWORD come from the provider. NOTE:
#      most managed offerings require TLS on their endpoint, and this app's
#      config does NOT currently enable spring.data.redis.ssl — that's a
#      real config gap to close first if going this route, not just an env
#      var swap.
REDIS_HOST=redis
REDIS_PORT=6379
REDIS_PASSWORD=
LOGSTREAM_TOPICS=server-topic,system-topic,app1-topic,app2-topic,app3-topic,app4-topic
# CRITICAL: must EXACTLY match the browser-visible office origin used to load the UI
# (scheme + host + non-default port, NO trailing slash). This value gates BOTH
# REST CORS and the WebSocket handshake (WebSocketConfig.setAllowedOrigins) — a
# mismatch makes every WS connection fail with 403 and no upgrade.
# Office deployment behind TLS by IP: https://10.0.0.5
# Office deployment by DNS:           https://logs.example.com
# Comma-separate to allow several origins.
LOGSTREAM_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://10.0.0.5
JVM_MAX_HEAP=512m

# Directory where downloadable log files live on the host. Files must be named
# {topic}.log and the topic must also be included in LOGSTREAM_TOPICS.
# e.g. server-topic -> /var/log/logstream/server-topic.log
LOGSTREAM_LOG_DIR=/var/log/logstream

# SSO — JWKS endpoint for JWT validation.
# Use the INTERNAL Docker hostname (keycloak), NOT the browser-visible server IP:
# the API fetches
# signing keys server-to-server inside the `monitoring` network. The token's
# issuer is the browser-visible URL, but with only jwk-set-uri configured Spring validates
# signature + expiry (not issuer), so the internal/public split is fine.
SSO_JWKS_URI=http://keycloak:8080/auth/realms/logstream/protocol/openid-connect/certs
